A||||1||SCCA FIERO||What the heck are those wires for?
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||05-15-99||11:06 PM||||On my 86 SE V6 4 speed. There are a couple of extra wires with a plug on the end just hanging there. Located in the wiring loom for the speedo that goes into the tranny. The same plce you check the transaxle fluid. Does anyone else have these? If so are they connected to something? My cruise doesn't work maybe they go to it. Any suggestions?
Z||000001||87FieroGT||05-16-99||01:35 AM||||Those extra wires are for the reverse swirch on the 5 speeds that were used in the Fieros. Either the Getrag or the Isuzu. They have the reverse switch built into the mechanics ov the tranny. I just recently traded an 86' SE 4 speed for my 87 GT and the 86 had those two wires also, but my 87 has a Getrag in it and that connection is used by the Tranny.
